To implement student attendance functionality using Stateful and Stateless widgets and setState().

Description:
This is the main experiment of the Student Attendance App because attendance information changes when the user marks a student as present or absent. Flutter provides StatefulWidget for interfaces whose data can change during application execution.

The attendance screen is implemented using a StatefulWidget. When the user clicks the Present button, the student's attendance status is changed and the attendance summary is updated. Similarly, clicking Absent changes the student's status. The setState() method tells Flutter that the state has changed and that the interface should be rebuilt with the updated information.

Reusable components such as student cards can be implemented as StatelessWidget when their appearance depends only on the data received from the parent.

The application can calculate the attendance percentage using classes attended and total classes. The user can also reset today's attendance information.

The lab manual specifically includes the assignment of building a Student Attendance Counter using setState(), making this experiment directly relevant to the project.

Used in the project:

StatefulWidget
StatelessWidget
setState()
Present/Absent buttons
Attendance counter
Attendance percentage
